<title>FINLAND: FINNISH REAL ESTATE TRADE INCREASED 8 PCT IN 1996.</title>
<headline>FINNISH REAL ESTATE TRADE INCREASED 8 PCT IN 1996.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish real estate trading increased eight percent last year to 57,000 transactions, the National Survey Board said in a statement received on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The value of real estate deals increased five percent to 14.2 billion markka, it said.</p>
<p>The statistics cover deals in developed and undeveloped land, but not transactions in apartments.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
